IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014, Part 2, ss 15 to 24: use, reservation and
-- restriction of business names, changes of name, address and particulars, deceased
-- registrants, cessation, cancellation and restoration.
-- Source: source/BNRA2014.txt lines 790 to 1179.

§ `Part 2 -- Registration: business names and changes`

§§ `15. Use of business names`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 15(1) and (2)"
GIVEN u IS A `Use of Name Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 15(1)` IF
        u's `the person is required to be registered`
    AND u's `the person is registered under this Act`
    AND u's `the person carries on business under a business name other than the registered business name`
    AND NOT u's `the person is not required to be registered in respect of that business name under section 4`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 15(3)"
GIVEN u IS A `Use of Name Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration authorises the use of the registered business name` IF
    NOT u's `use of the registered business name is otherwise prohibited under a written law or other law`

§§ `16. Reservation of business names`

-- 16(3)(b) turns on the Registrar being satisfied.  The Minister's certificate under
-- s 13(1) is conclusive only "for the purposes of sections 9(b) and 12(1)(a)(ii)", so it
-- is not read into s 16.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 16(3)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN r IS A `Reservation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` IF
        (r's `public interest facts`)'s `the Registrar is satisfied that the business is likely to be used, or is used or intended to be used, for an unlawful purpose or for purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order in Singapore`
     OR (r's `public interest facts`)'s `the Registrar is satisfied that it would be contrary to the national security or interest`
     OR r's `the application is by or on behalf of a foreign company not registered under Division 2 of Part 11 of the Companies Act 1967`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 16(1) and (2)"
GIVEN r IS A `Reservation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may approve the reservation` IF
        r's `the application is lodged with the Registrar`
    AND r's `the application is made in good faith`
    AND r's `the name is one in respect of which the person may be registered having regard to section 17(1), (2) and (3)`
    AND NOT `the Registrar must refuse to approve the reservation` r

-- 16(4): the reservation starts when the Registrar receives the application.  If
-- approved it ends 60 days after the applicant is notified, or after each further period
-- of 60 days the Registrar extends it by; if refused, on the date the applicant is
-- notified of the refusal (NOTES.md fork F2).

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 16(4)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Reservation Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the reservation` MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `decision`
    WHEN `approved` notified extensions THEN notified PLUS (60 TIMES (1 PLUS extensions))
    WHEN `refused` notified THEN notified

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 16(4)"
GIVEN r IS A `Reservation Facts`
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name is reserved on the date` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST r's `the date the Registrar receives the application`
    AND `the date` AT MOST `the last day of the reservation` r

-- 16(5): appeal to the Minister within 30 days after being informed, against a refusal
-- to approve or to extend: `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days`
-- (bnra-part2-registration.l4) answers it.

§§ `17. Restrictions on registration of business names`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(1)(a) to (d)"
GIVEN n IS A `Name Restriction Facts`
      `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(1) bars the name` IF
        NOT n's `the Minister has consented`
    AND (   n's `the name is undesirable in the Registrar's opinion`
         OR (    n's `the name is identical to any other registered business name, or to the name of a corporation or limited partnership`
             AND NOT `section 17(3) permits registration of the name`)
         OR n's `the name is identical to a name reserved under section 16 of this Act or under a listed provision of the Companies Act 1967, the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 or the Limited Partnerships Act 2008`
         OR n's `the name is of a kind the Minister has directed the Registrar, by notification in the Gazette, not to accept for registration`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(2)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Earlier Use of Name`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` MEANS
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `the business name of a person whose registration was cancelled under this Act or has ceased under section 22` d THEN 1
    WHEN `the name of a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` d THEN 2
    WHEN `the name of a company dissolved following its name being struck off under section 344 or 344A of the Companies Act 1967` d THEN 6
    WHEN `the name of a foreign company of whose dissolution notice has been given under section 377(2) of the Companies Act 1967` d THEN 2
    WHEN `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up` d THEN 2
    WHEN `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` d THEN 6
    WHEN `the name of a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` d THEN 1
    WHEN `the name of a limited partnership dissolved under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` d THEN 1

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(2)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Earlier Use of Name`
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the earlier use of the name ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `the business name of a person whose registration was cancelled under this Act or has ceased under section 22` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a company dissolved following its winding up under Part 8 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a company dissolved following its name being struck off under section 344 or 344A of the Companies Act 1967` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a foreign company of whose dissolution notice has been given under section 377(2) of the Companies Act 1967` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its winding up` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a limited liability partnership dissolved following its name being struck off under section 63 of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a limited partnership whose registration was cancelled under section 14(1) or 19(4) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` d THEN d
    WHEN `the name of a limited partnership dissolved under section 19(2) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008` d THEN d

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(2)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Earlier Use of Name`
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
      `the Minister has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(2) bars the name` IF
        NOT `the Minister has consented`
    AND `the date of the application`
        LESS THAN `add months` (`the date the earlier use of the name ended` u) (12 TIMES `the waiting period in years after an earlier use of the name` u)

-- 17(3): the Registrar may register a name identical to that of a foreign company that
-- ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business (3 months after cessation),
-- or whose name was struck off (6 years after), or of a limited partnership that ceased
-- to carry on business in Singapore (one year after).  The two limbs of (3)(a) are joined
-- by "and": read as alternatives (NOTES.md fork F3).

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(3)(a)(i), (a)(ii) and (b)"
GIVEN p IS A `Permitted Earlier Use`
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17(3) permits registration of the name` IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the name of a foreign company that lodged notice under section 377(1) of the Companies Act 1967 that it ceased to have a place of business or to carry on business in Singapore` d THEN
        `the date of the application` AT LEAST `add months` d 3
    WHEN `the name of a foreign company struck off under section 377(8), (9) or (10) of the Companies Act 1967` d THEN
        `the date of the application` AT LEAST `add months` d (12 TIMES 6)
    WHEN `the name of a limited partnership that lodged notice under section 19(1) of the Limited Partnerships Act 2008 that it ceased to carry on business in Singapore` d THEN
        `the date of the application` AT LEAST `add months` d 12

-- 17(4): the Registrar may direct a change of name on any of five grounds, and the person
-- must comply within 6 weeks or a longer period the Registrar allows.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(4)(a) to (e)"
GIVEN g IS A `Direction Grounds Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may direct the person to change the registered business name` IF
        g's `the name is not permitted to be registered under section 17(1)(a), (b) or (d)`
     OR g's `the name is not permitted under section 17(2) until the relevant period has expired`
     OR g's `the name is permitted under section 17(3) only after the relevant period has expired`
     OR g's `the name so nearly resembles the name of a corporation or limited partnership, or a registered business name, as to be likely to be mistaken for it`
     OR g's `the use of the name has been restrained by an injunction granted under the Trade Marks Act 1998`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(4)"
GIVEN d IS A `Direction Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` MEANS
    LET sixweeks MEANS d's `the date of the Registrar's direction` PLUS 42 IN
        CONSIDER d's `the date to which the Registrar has allowed a longer period, if any`
        WHEN JUST allowed THEN (IF allowed GREATER THAN sixweeks THEN allowed ELSE sixweeks)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN sixweeks

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(4)"
GIVEN d IS A `Direction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person complied with the direction in time` IF
    CONSIDER d's `the date the person changes the registered business name, if it has been changed`
    WHEN JUST changed THEN changed AT MOST `the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(4)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to change the registered business name as directed` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `change the registered business name as the Registrar directed`
    WITHIN 42
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the registered business name was not changed within 6 weeks after the direction, as section 17(4) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(8)"
GIVEN d IS A `Direction Facts`
      `the date the Registrar proposes to cancel` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel for failure to comply with the direction` IF
        `the date the Registrar proposes to cancel` GREATER THAN `the last day for complying with the Registrar's direction` d
    AND NOT `the person complied with the direction in time` d

-- 17(7): on the ground in (4)(d) the Registrar is not to consider an application from
-- any person (17(6)) unless received within 12 months after the person was registered
-- in respect of the name, or the change of name was approved.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 17(6) and (7)"
GIVEN d IS A `Direction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may consider the application for a direction` IF
    IF d's `the ground of the application is that the name so nearly resembles another name as to be likely to be mistaken for it`
    THEN d's `the date the Registrar receives an application under section 17(6)` AT MOST `add months` (d's `the date the person was registered in respect of the name, or the change of name was approved`) 12
    ELSE TRUE

-- 17(5) (the power applies whether or not the name was registered through inadvertence
-- and whenever registered) and 17(10) (the Registrar and the Minister must accept as
-- correct the General Division's grant of an injunction, "to avoid doubt"): inert.
-- 17(9) is answered by `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days`.

§§ `18. Change of registered business name`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 18(3) and s 17(1), (2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Name Change Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse the change of registered business name` IF
        c's `the new name is one the Registrar must refuse under section 17`
    AND NOT c's `the Minister has consented`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 18(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Name Change Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar is to issue a notice of change of registered business name` IF
        c's `the application to change the registered business name is lodged with the Registrar`
    AND c's `the Registrar approves the application`
    AND NOT `the Registrar must refuse the change of registered business name` c

§§ `19. Change of residential address`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 19(1)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Address Change Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual must lodge a notice of the new residential address` IF
    CONSIDER a's `kind of holder`
    WHEN `a registered individual proprietor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a partner of a registered firm who is an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an authorised representative` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 19(1)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Address Change Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for lodging the notice of the new residential address` MEANS
    a's `the date of the change of residential address` PLUS 14

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 19(2)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Address Change Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is taken to have informed the Registrar of the change of residential address` IF
    a's `the individual has made a report of the change under section 10 of the National Registration Act 1965`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 19(1)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to lodge a notice of the new residential address` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `lodge a notice of the new residential address`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the notice of the new residential address was not lodged within 14 days after the change, as section 19(1) requires"

§§ `20. Registration of change in particulars`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Particulars Change Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(1) applies to the change` IF
    CONSIDER c's `kind of change`
    WHEN `a change of the residential address of a registered individual proprietor, of a partner of a registered firm who is an individual, or of an authorised representative` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a change of a registered business name` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a change in any other registered particular` THEN TRUE

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(1)"
GIVEN c IS A `Particulars Change Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for lodging the notice of the change in particulars` MEANS
    LET fourteen MEANS c's `the date of the change` PLUS 14 IN
        CONSIDER c's `the last day the Registrar has allowed, on application, for lodging the notice`
        WHEN JUST allowed THEN (IF allowed GREATER THAN fourteen THEN allowed ELSE fourteen)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN fourteen

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(1)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to lodge a notice of the change in particulars` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `lodge a notice of the change in particulars`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the notice of the change in particulars was not lodged within 14 days after the change, as section 20(1) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(3)"
GIVEN c IS A `Partner Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for lodging the notice of a partner's cessation` MEANS
    c's `the date the person ceased to be a partner of the registered firm` PLUS 14

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(3)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty of the former partner and the continuing partners to lodge a notice of cessation` MEANS
    PARTY `The continuing partners`
    MUST `lodge a notice of a partner's cessation`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The continuing partners` BECAUSE "the notice of the partner's cessation was not lodged within 14 days after the cessation, as section 20(3) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 20(4)"
GIVEN c IS A `Partner Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other persons may lodge the notice without the person who cannot be found` IF
        c's `the person required to lodge the notice cannot be located or found`
    AND c's `the Registrar has allowed the other persons required to lodge the notice to do so`

-- 20(5): the Registrar may require a notice to be verified: a power with no condition,
-- inert.

§§ `21. Deceased registrants`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 21(1)(a), (b), (c) and (2)"
GIVEN d IS A `Deceased Registrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may permit the person to lodge a notice on behalf of the deceased` IF
        d's `the deceased was a registered individual proprietor or a partner of a registered firm who is an individual`
    AND (   d's `the person is the personal representative of the deceased`
         OR d's `the person would, in the Registrar's opinion, be entitled to apply to court for an order for the administration by the court of the deceased's estate`)
    AND d's `the person has provided evidence acceptable to the Registrar`

§§ `22. Cessation of business`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 22(1)"
GIVEN c IS A `Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for lodging the notice of cessation of business` MEANS
    c's `the date the person stopped` PLUS 14

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 22(1)"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`the duty to lodge a notice of cessation of business` MEANS
    PARTY `The registrant`
    MUST `lodge a notice of cessation of business`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `The registrant` BECAUSE "the notice of cessation of business was not lodged within 14 days after stopping, as section 22(1) requires"

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 22(2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered person may lodge a notice in advance` IF
    c's `the Registrar has allowed the person to lodge an advance notice`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 22(3)"
GIVEN c IS A `Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered person is guilty of an offence under section 22(3)` IF
        c's `the registered person stops carrying on business in Singapore under the registered business name`
    AND (CONSIDER c's `the date the person lodges the notice of cessation, if it has been lodged`
         WHEN JUST lodged THEN lodged GREATER THAN `the last day for lodging the notice of cessation of business` c
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 22(4)"
GIVEN c IS A `Cessation Facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date the registration ceases` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the date specified in the advance notice as the date of stopping, if any`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN JUST specified
    WHEN NOTHING THEN c's `the date the person lodges the notice of cessation, if it has been lodged`

§§ `23. Cancellation of registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 23(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN n IS A `Non-trading Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may give notice proposing to cancel` IF
    n's `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the registered person is not carrying on business in Singapore in respect of the registered business name`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 23(1)(b)"
GIVEN n IS A `Non-trading Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice allows enough time for objection` IF
    n's `the date specified in the notice for delivering any objection` AT LEAST n's `the date of the notice` PLUS 30

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 23(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN n IS A `Non-trading Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 23` IF
        `the Registrar may give notice proposing to cancel` n
    AND n's `the Registrar gave the person written notice stating the proposal to cancel and the date by which any objection must be delivered`
    AND `the notice allows enough time for objection` n
    AND (   n's `the person has answered that the person is not carrying on business under the registered business name`
         OR (CONSIDER n's `the date the Registrar received a written objection, if any`
             WHEN JUST received THEN received GREATER THAN n's `the date of the notice` PLUS 30
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE))

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 23(3)"
GIVEN `the registration is cancelled under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any certificate or notice pertaining to the registration is taken to be cancelled` IF
    `the registration is cancelled under section 23`

§§ `24. Restoration of registration`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 24(1)"
GIVEN r IS A `Restoration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may apply to restore the registration` IF
    CONSIDER r's `how the registration ended`
    WHEN `cancelled under section 12(2)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancelled under section 14` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancelled under section 23` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ceased under section 22` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ended in another way` THEN FALSE

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 24(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Restoration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application to restore is made in time` IF
        r's `the date the application to restore is lodged` AT MOST `add months` (r's `the date the registration was cancelled or ceased`) 12
     OR r's `the Registrar allows a longer time in special circumstances`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 24(3)"
GIVEN r IS A `Restoration Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may grant the application to restore` IF
        `the person may apply to restore the registration` r
    AND `the application to restore is made in time` r
    AND NOT r's `a restriction against registration under section 9 applies`
    AND r's `the outstanding renewal fees have been paid`
    AND r's `the prescribed late renewal penalty has been paid`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 24(4)"
GIVEN `the Registrar grants the application to restore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration is treated as if it had not been cancelled or had not ceased` IF
    `the Registrar grants the application to restore`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 24(5)"
`restoration prevents prosecution for an offence under section 35(1)(a)` MEANS FALSE
